-- CONTROL for i4-xmod-method-level-slot-rejected.
--
-- SPEC ANSWER, HAND-DERIVED: with `zmod`'s own `impl Sizer Int` present,
-- `match(IE, zmod.Sizer Int)` is the singleton {`zmod`'s impl}, trivially its own
-- ⊑-minimum, so §3 `inst` selects it and `peek Cell 3` = `bulk 3` = 3 + 7 = 10.
-- Prints `10`.
--
-- 🚨 `10` IS A VALUE ONLY `zmod`'s IMPL CAN PRODUCE — `amod`'s `weight n = n * 100`
-- would give `300`.  So the pair separates "the reject was removed" from "the wrong
-- impl was selected", which a verdict-only control cannot.
--
-- ⚠️ It rules out the duller readings of the sibling's reject, each of which would
-- predict a reject HERE too: "a method-level `=>` slot cannot be discharged at all
-- across modules"; "any same-spelled interface in the graph poisons the goal";
-- "`Holder`'s impl cannot see `Sizer`".  None survives `10`.
--
-- ⚠️ BEHAVES IDENTICALLY ON BOTH ARMS, deliberately and stated so it is not
-- mistaken for coverage of #1446: a goal with exactly one candidate is not a witness
-- to an identity re-key.  Two edits from the sibling, not one — see `amod.mdk`.
import amod
import zmod.{Cell(..), useCell}

main = println (useCell 3)
